      "text": "The Sahara also used to be a lush wet landscape too. More info: \n\n• Cyclic Shifts: The Sahara switches between desert and green savanna (known as African Humid Periods) due to Earth's orbital precession and axial tilt every ~21,000 to 26,000 years.\n\n• Prior Green Periods: This pattern has repeated more than 230 times over the last 8 million years, meaning the region was green during earlier windows long before the famous Holocene Green Sahara (which lasted roughly from 11,000 to 5,000 years ago).",
